Build Trainer and Downloader on Linux

LoRATrainer passes optional base addresses to memset, which glibc declares
non-optional. Its largest openStore closure needs an explicit signature, or
swiftc 6.0.3 takes too long to type-check it.

DownloaderSupport imports CryptoKit and Darwin. It now uses swift-crypto and
a guarded Glibc import. The CFNetwork and resume-data userInfo keys are
written as literal strings, autoreleasepool is a no-op when ObjectiveC is
absent, and the waitsForConnectivity assignment is dropped because the
property is get-only in corelibs-foundation.
